IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `soca-dates`

-- Survival of Causes of Action Act 1940 (SA) -- the rules, seat-neutral. The claimant's seat (soca-seat.l4) asks the
-- questions and restates none of these rules. One regulative rule (s 4(b), proceedings within six months after the
-- grant) is run by EVALTRACE.
--
-- Answers are named outcomes. Where the text says no in its own words ("does not apply", "shall not include", "No
-- proceedings shall be maintainable ... unless") the outcome begins "no:"; where the text is silent it begins "not
-- covered:" or "s N does not ..." (the 2026-11-04 and 2026-11-05 rulings, in substance).
--
-- Based on content from the South Australian Legislation website at 6 November 2026 (version of 8 February 2006).
-- CC BY 4.0. BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Survival of Causes of Action Act 1940 (SA)`

§§ `s 2 and s 5: which causes of action survive death`

-- "cause of action": a right to sue (a borrowed term, asked as a fact).
-- "survives for the benefit of his or her estate": the executor or administrator may sue on it, and what is recovered
-- goes into the estate.

DECLARE `Survival for the estate answer` IS ONE OF
    `yes: the cause of action survives for the benefit of the estate of the person who died (s 2(1)(a))`
    `no: a cause of action in defamation does not survive for the estate (s 2(2))`
    `not covered: s 2(1)(a) speaks only of a cause of action vested in the person at the time of death`

-- s 2(1)(a), (2).
GIVEN `a cause of action was vested in them at death` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is in defamation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Survival for the estate answer`
`does it survive for the estate (s 2(1)(a), (2))` `a cause of action was vested in them at death` `it is in defamation` MEANS
    IF NOT `a cause of action was vested in them at death`
    THEN `not covered: s 2(1)(a) speaks only of a cause of action vested in the person at the time of death`
    ELSE IF `it is in defamation`
         THEN `no: a cause of action in defamation does not survive for the estate (s 2(2))`
         ELSE `yes: the cause of action survives for the benefit of the estate of the person who died (s 2(1)(a))`

DECLARE `Survival against the estate answer` IS ONE OF
    `yes: the cause of action survives against the estate of the person who died (s 2(1)(b))`
    `yes: the person who died before or with the damage is deemed to have been liable before death, and the cause of action survives against the estate (ss 5, 2(1)(b))`
    `no: a cause of action in defamation does not survive against the estate (s 2(2))`
    `not covered: s 2(1)(b) and s 5 speak only of a cause of action existing against the person at death, or one that would have existed had they not died before or with the damage`

-- s 5: "Where damage has been suffered by reason of any act or omission in respect of which a cause of action would
-- have subsisted against any person if that person had not died before or at the same time as the damage was
-- suffered, there shall be deemed ... to have been subsisting against him before his death such cause of action".
GIVEN `the damage was suffered after or at their death` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a cause of action would have subsisted had they not died first` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is deemed to have subsisted before death (s 5)` IF
        `the damage was suffered after or at their death`
    AND `a cause of action would have subsisted had they not died first`

-- s 2(1)(b), (2), s 5.
GIVEN `a cause of action existed against them at death` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the damage was suffered after or at their death` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a cause of action would have subsisted had they not died first` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is in defamation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Survival against the estate answer`
`does it survive against the estate (ss 2(1)(b), (2), 5)` `a cause of action existed against them at death` `the damage was suffered after or at their death` `a cause of action would have subsisted had they not died first` `it is in defamation` MEANS
    IF NOT (`a cause of action existed against them at death` OR `is deemed to have subsisted before death (s 5)` `the damage was suffered after or at their death` `a cause of action would have subsisted had they not died first`)
    THEN `not covered: s 2(1)(b) and s 5 speak only of a cause of action existing against the person at death, or one that would have existed had they not died before or with the damage`
    ELSE IF `it is in defamation`
         THEN `no: a cause of action in defamation does not survive against the estate (s 2(2))`
         ELSE IF `a cause of action existed against them at death`
              THEN `yes: the cause of action survives against the estate of the person who died (s 2(1)(b))`
              ELSE `yes: the person who died before or with the damage is deemed to have been liable before death, and the cause of action survives against the estate (ss 5, 2(1)(b))`

GIVEN `a cause of action existed against them at death` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the damage was suffered after or at their death` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a cause of action would have subsisted had they not died first` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is in defamation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `it survives against the estate` `a cause of action existed against them at death` `the damage was suffered after or at their death` `a cause of action would have subsisted had they not died first` `it is in defamation` IF
    CONSIDER `does it survive against the estate (ss 2(1)(b), (2), 5)` `a cause of action existed against them at death` `the damage was suffered after or at their death` `a cause of action would have subsisted had they not died first` `it is in defamation`
    WHEN `yes: the cause of action survives against the estate of the person who died (s 2(1)(b))` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `yes: the person who died before or with the damage is deemed to have been liable before death, and the cause of action survives against the estate (ss 5, 2(1)(b))` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `s 3: the damages the estate recovers`

-- s 3(3) "dust-related condition": (a) a disease specified in the Schedule, or (b) any other pathological condition of
-- the lungs, pleura or peritoneum that is attributable to dust.
DECLARE `Condition` IS ONE OF
    `aluminosis`
    `asbestosis`
    `asbestos induced carcinoma`
    `asbestos related pleural diseases`
    `bagassosis`
    `berylliosis`
    `byssinosis`
    `coal dust pneumoconiosis`
    `farmers lung`
    `hard metal pneumoconiosis`
    `mesothelioma`
    `silicosis`
    `silico-tuberculosis`
    `talcosis`
    `another condition of the lungs, pleura or peritoneum`
    `another condition`

GIVEN `the condition` IS A `Condition`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a prescribed dust disease (Schedule)` IF
    CONSIDER `the condition`
    WHEN `another condition of the lungs, pleura or peritoneum` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `another condition` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- s 3(3): the definition is a "means", so a condition that meets neither limb is not a dust-related condition.
GIVEN `the condition` IS A `Condition`
      `it is attributable to dust` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a dust-related condition (s 3(3))` IF
        `is a prescribed dust disease (Schedule)` `the condition`
    OR  (`the condition` EQUALS `another condition of the lungs, pleura or peritoneum` AND `it is attributable to dust`)

-- s 3(2): "if a person commences an action for damages in respect of a dust-related condition and dies as a result of
-- that condition before the action is finally determined".
GIVEN `the condition` IS A `Condition`
      `it is attributable to dust` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they commenced an action for damages for it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they died as a result of it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the action was finally determined before death` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 3(2) applies` IF
        `is a dust-related condition (s 3(3))` `the condition` `it is attributable to dust`
    AND `they commenced an action for damages for it`
    AND `they died as a result of it`
    AND (NOT `the action was finally determined before death`)

-- s 3(2) asked ahead of death by the person with the condition: what s 3(2) would do if they died of it before their
-- action is finally determined.
DECLARE `Dust condition estate answer` IS ONE OF
    `yes: if you die of it before your action is finally determined, your estate recovers damages for pain and suffering, bodily and mental harm, curtailment of expectation of life, and exemplary damages (s 3(2))`
    `not yet: s 3(2) applies only once you have commenced an action for damages for the condition`
    `no: it is not a dust-related condition (s 3(3)), so s 3(2) does not apply and s 3(1) excludes those damages from what your estate recovers`

GIVEN `the condition` IS A `Condition`
      `it is attributable to dust` IS A BOOLEAN
      `you have commenced an action for damages for it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Dust condition estate answer`
`would s 3(2) keep those damages for the estate` `the condition` `it is attributable to dust` `you have commenced an action for damages for it` MEANS
    IF NOT (`is a dust-related condition (s 3(3))` `the condition` `it is attributable to dust`)
    THEN `no: it is not a dust-related condition (s 3(3)), so s 3(2) does not apply and s 3(1) excludes those damages from what your estate recovers`
    ELSE IF `you have commenced an action for damages for it`
         THEN `yes: if you die of it before your action is finally determined, your estate recovers damages for pain and suffering, bodily and mental harm, curtailment of expectation of life, and exemplary damages (s 3(2))`
         ELSE `not yet: s 3(2) applies only once you have commenced an action for damages for the condition`

DECLARE `Head of damages` IS ONE OF
    `pain or suffering`
    `bodily or mental harm`
    `the curtailment of expectation of life`
    `loss of earning capacity or future earnings for the years lost`
    `exemplary damages`
    `funeral expenses`
    `a loss or gain to the estate consequent on the death`
    `other damages`

DECLARE `Estate damages answer` IS ONE OF
    `no: the estate does not recover it, because the cause of action does not survive for the benefit of the estate (s 2)`
    `no: s 3(1)(a) excludes it from the damages recoverable for the benefit of the estate`
    `no: s 3(1)(a)(iv) excludes earnings for the years lost, and the dust-related condition exception in s 3(2) does not restore them`
    `no: s 3(1)(b) excludes exemplary damages`
    `yes: s 3(2) lets the estate recover it, because the person started an action for a dust-related condition and died of that condition before the action was finally determined`
    `no: the wrong caused the death, so the damages are calculated without reference to a loss or gain to the estate consequent on the death (s 3(1)(d))`
    `yes, it may be included: the wrong caused the death, and a sum for funeral expenses may be included (s 3(1)(d))`
    `s 3 does not exclude it: the estate recovers it as the general law of damages allows`
    `not covered: s 3(1)(d) applies only where the wrong caused the death; the Act does not otherwise deal with it`

-- s 3(1), (2). Applies only "Where a cause of action survives as aforesaid for the benefit of the estate".
GIVEN `the head` IS A `Head of damages`
      `it survives for the estate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the wrong caused the death` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the dust-related condition exception applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Estate damages answer`
`can the estate recover that head (s 3)` `the head` `it survives for the estate` `the wrong caused the death` `the dust-related condition exception applies` MEANS
    IF NOT `it survives for the estate`
    THEN `no: the estate does not recover it, because the cause of action does not survive for the benefit of the estate (s 2)`
    ELSE CONSIDER `the head`
         WHEN `pain or suffering` THEN `the s 3(1)(a) head, unless s 3(2)`
         WHEN `bodily or mental harm` THEN `the s 3(1)(a) head, unless s 3(2)`
         WHEN `the curtailment of expectation of life` THEN `the s 3(1)(a) head, unless s 3(2)`
         WHEN `loss of earning capacity or future earnings for the years lost` THEN `no: s 3(1)(a)(iv) excludes earnings for the years lost, and the dust-related condition exception in s 3(2) does not restore them`
         WHEN `exemplary damages` THEN
             IF `the dust-related condition exception applies`
             THEN `yes: s 3(2) lets the estate recover it, because the person started an action for a dust-related condition and died of that condition before the action was finally determined`
             ELSE `no: s 3(1)(b) excludes exemplary damages`
         WHEN `funeral expenses` THEN
             IF `the wrong caused the death`
             THEN `yes, it may be included: the wrong caused the death, and a sum for funeral expenses may be included (s 3(1)(d))`
             ELSE `not covered: s 3(1)(d) applies only where the wrong caused the death; the Act does not otherwise deal with it`
         WHEN `a loss or gain to the estate consequent on the death` THEN
             IF `the wrong caused the death`
             THEN `no: the wrong caused the death, so the damages are calculated without reference to a loss or gain to the estate consequent on the death (s 3(1)(d))`
             ELSE `not covered: s 3(1)(d) applies only where the wrong caused the death; the Act does not otherwise deal with it`
         WHEN `other damages` THEN `s 3 does not exclude it: the estate recovers it as the general law of damages allows`
    WHERE
        `the s 3(1)(a) head, unless s 3(2)` MEANS
            IF `the dust-related condition exception applies`
            THEN `yes: s 3(2) lets the estate recover it, because the person started an action for a dust-related condition and died of that condition before the action was finally determined`
            ELSE `no: s 3(1)(a) excludes it from the damages recoverable for the benefit of the estate`

§§ `s 4: proceedings in tort against the estate`

-- s 4: "No proceedings shall be maintainable in respect of a cause of action in tort which by virtue of this Act has
-- survived against the estate of a deceased person, unless either-- (a) proceedings against him in respect of that
-- cause of action were pending at the date of his death; or (b) the cause of action arose not earlier than six months
-- before his death and proceedings are taken in respect thereof not later than six months after his executor or
-- administrator took out probate or letters of administration."

-- (b), first limb: the earliest day the cause of action may have arisen (fork F1).
GIVEN `the day of death` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the earliest day the cause of action may have arisen (s 4(b))` `the day of death` MEANS
    `the day of death` `moved by months` (0 MINUS 6)

GIVEN `the day it arose` IS A DATE, `the day of death` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `it arose not earlier than six months before the death (s 4(b))` IF
    (`the earliest day the cause of action may have arisen (s 4(b))` `the day of death`) `is on or before` `the day it arose`

-- (b), second limb: the last day for taking proceedings (fork F1).
GIVEN `the day of the grant` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day to take proceedings (s 4(b))` `the day of the grant` MEANS
    `the day of the grant` `moved by months` 6

DECLARE `Estate party` IS ONE OF `the claimant`

DECLARE `Estate act` IS ONE OF `take proceedings against the estate`

-- s 4(b) as a regulative rule. Clock: day 0 is the day the executor or administrator took out probate or letters of
-- administration.
GIVEN `the days allowed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Estate party` `Estate act`
`s 4(b) -- proceedings must be taken not later than six months after the grant` `the days allowed` MEANS
    PARTY  `the claimant`
    MUST   `take proceedings against the estate`
    WITHIN `the days allowed`
    LEST   BREACH BY `the claimant` BECAUSE "s 4(b): proceedings were not taken within six months after probate or letters of administration were taken out"

DECLARE `Six months answer` IS ONE OF
    `in time`
    `out of time`
    `still in time`

-- On the stable l4 a CONSIDER on an EVALTRACE matches FULFILLED but not BREACH: where proceedings were taken, FULFILLED
-- means in time and anything else late; where they were not, the question is whether taking them today would still be
-- in time. Proceedings taken on or before the day of the grant are "not later than six months after" it (fork F2), and
-- are answered without a trace.
GIVEN `the day of the grant` IS A DATE
      `proceedings have been taken` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day proceedings were taken` IS A DATE
      `today` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Six months answer`
`were proceedings taken within six months after the grant (s 4(b))` `the day of the grant` `proceedings have been taken` `the day proceedings were taken` `today` MEANS
    IF `proceedings have been taken`
    THEN IF `the day proceedings were taken` `is on or before` `the day of the grant`
         THEN `in time`
         ELSE CONSIDER EVALTRACE `the rule` 0 (LIST (EVENT `the claimant` `take proceedings against the estate` (`the days from` `the day of the grant` `to` `the day proceedings were taken`)))
              WHEN FULFILLED THEN `in time`
              OTHERWISE `out of time`
    ELSE IF `today` `is on or before` `the day of the grant`
         THEN `still in time`
         ELSE CONSIDER EVALTRACE `the rule` 0 (LIST (EVENT `the claimant` `take proceedings against the estate` (`the days from` `the day of the grant` `to` `today`)))
              WHEN FULFILLED THEN `still in time`
              OTHERWISE `out of time`
    WHERE
        `the rule` MEANS `s 4(b) -- proceedings must be taken not later than six months after the grant` (`the days from` `the day of the grant` `to` (`the last day to take proceedings (s 4(b))` `the day of the grant`))

DECLARE `Proceedings against the estate answer` IS ONE OF
    `no: a cause of action in defamation does not survive, so there is nothing to sue the estate on (s 2(2))`
    `not covered: no cause of action existed against the person at death, and s 5 does not apply`
    `s 4 does not apply: the cause of action is not in tort; it survives against the estate (s 2(1)(b)) and s 4 sets no condition on it`
    `yes: proceedings against the person were pending at the date of death (s 4(a))`
    `no: the cause of action arose more than six months before the death and no proceedings were pending at the death, so no proceedings are maintainable (s 4)`
    `not yet: the six months in s 4(b) have not begun, because no probate or letters of administration have been taken out`
    `yes: the cause of action arose not earlier than six months before the death and proceedings were taken not later than six months after the grant (s 4(b))`
    `still in time: proceedings must be taken not later than six months after the grant (s 4(b))`
    `no: proceedings were not taken within six months after the grant, so no proceedings are maintainable (s 4(b))`

GIVEN `a cause of action existed against them at death` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the damage was suffered after or at their death` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a cause of action would have subsisted had they not died first` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is in defamation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is in tort` IS A BOOLEAN
      `proceedings were pending at death` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day it arose` IS A DATE
      `the day of death` IS A DATE
      `a grant has been taken out` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day of the grant` IS A DATE
      `proceedings have been taken` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day proceedings were taken` IS A DATE
      `today` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Proceedings against the estate answer`
`are proceedings against the estate maintainable (s 4)` `a cause of action existed against them at death` `the damage was suffered after or at their death` `a cause of action would have subsisted had they not died first` `it is in defamation` `it is in tort` `proceedings were pending at death` `the day it arose` `the day of death` `a grant has been taken out` `the day of the grant` `proceedings have been taken` `the day proceedings were taken` `today` MEANS
    IF NOT (`a cause of action existed against them at death` OR `is deemed to have subsisted before death (s 5)` `the damage was suffered after or at their death` `a cause of action would have subsisted had they not died first`)
    THEN `not covered: no cause of action existed against the person at death, and s 5 does not apply`
    ELSE IF `it is in defamation`
         THEN `no: a cause of action in defamation does not survive, so there is nothing to sue the estate on (s 2(2))`
         ELSE IF NOT `it is in tort`
              THEN `s 4 does not apply: the cause of action is not in tort; it survives against the estate (s 2(1)(b)) and s 4 sets no condition on it`
              ELSE IF `proceedings were pending at death`
                   THEN `yes: proceedings against the person were pending at the date of death (s 4(a))`
                   ELSE IF NOT (`it arose not earlier than six months before the death (s 4(b))` `the day it arose` `the day of death`)
                        THEN `no: the cause of action arose more than six months before the death and no proceedings were pending at the death, so no proceedings are maintainable (s 4)`
                        ELSE IF NOT `a grant has been taken out`
                             THEN `not yet: the six months in s 4(b) have not begun, because no probate or letters of administration have been taken out`
                             ELSE CONSIDER `were proceedings taken within six months after the grant (s 4(b))` `the day of the grant` `proceedings have been taken` `the day proceedings were taken` `today`
                                  WHEN `in time` THEN `yes: the cause of action arose not earlier than six months before the death and proceedings were taken not later than six months after the grant (s 4(b))`
                                  WHEN `still in time` THEN `still in time: proceedings must be taken not later than six months after the grant (s 4(b))`
                                  WHEN `out of time` THEN `no: proceedings were not taken within six months after the grant, so no proceedings are maintainable (s 4(b))`

§§ `s 6: other rights saved`

DECLARE `Dependants answer` IS ONE OF
    `no: this Act does not take away the dependants' right to bring an action for the death (s 6(1)); that action is separate from the estate's surviving claim`
    `not covered: s 6(1) speaks only of the dependants of the person who died`

GIVEN `you are a dependant` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Dependants answer`
`does the surviving claim affect the dependants' action (s 6(1))` `you are a dependant` MEANS
    IF `you are a dependant`
    THEN `no: this Act does not take away the dependants' right to bring an action for the death (s 6(1)); that action is separate from the estate's surviving claim`
    ELSE `not covered: s 6(1) speaks only of the dependants of the person who died`

DECLARE `Contributory negligence answer` IS ONE OF
    `yes: the Law Reform (Contributory Negligence and Apportionment of Liability) Act 2001 applies to the surviving cause of action (s 6(2))`
    `not covered: s 6(2) speaks only of a cause of action that survives for or against an estate under this Act`

GIVEN `it survives under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Contributory negligence answer`
`does the apportionment Act apply (s 6(2))` `it survives under this Act` MEANS
    IF `it survives under this Act`
    THEN `yes: the Law Reform (Contributory Negligence and Apportionment of Liability) Act 2001 applies to the surviving cause of action (s 6(2))`
    ELSE `not covered: s 6(2) speaks only of a cause of action that survives for or against an estate under this Act`
